      "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an irreducible, geometrically unibranch scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a prime number and <MATH_0003>. Let <MATH_0004>\nbe a Noetherian ring. Let <MATH_0005> be a finite type,\nlocally constant sheaf of <MATH_0006>-modules on <MATH_0007>\nwhich is annihilated by <MATH_0008>. Then there exists a\nfinite <ACCENT_0001>tale morphism <MATH_0009> of degree prime to <MATH_0010>\nsuch that <MATH_0011> has a finite filtration whose\nsuccessive quotients are of the form <MATH_0012>\nfor some finite <MATH_0013>-modules <MATH_0014>.\n",
