          "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14",
          "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nChoose a geometric point <MATH_0001> of <MATH_0002>.\nVia the equivalence of Lemma <REF_0001>\nthe sheaf <MATH_0003> corresponds to a finite dimensional\n<MATH_0004>-vector space <MATH_0005> with a continuous\n<MATH_0006>-action.\nLet <MATH_0007> be the image of the homomorphism\n<MATH_0008> giving the action.\nObserve that <MATH_0009> is finite.\nThe surjective continuous homomorphism\n<MATH_0010>\ncorresponds to a Galois object <MATH_0011> of\n<MATH_0012> with automorphism group <MATH_0013>, see\nFundamental Groups, Section <REF_0002>.\nLet <MATH_0014> be an <MATH_0015>-Sylow subgroup.\nWe claim that <MATH_0016> works. Namely, let <MATH_0017>\nbe a geometric point over <MATH_0018>. The image of\n<MATH_0019>\nis <MATH_0020> as follows from the functorial\nnature of fundamental groups. Hence the action of <MATH_0021>\non <MATH_0022> corresponding to <MATH_0023> is through\nthe map <MATH_0024>, see\nRemark <REF_0003>. As\n<MATH_0025> is a finite <MATH_0026>-group, the irreducible constituents of the\nrepresentation <MATH_0027>\nare each trivial of rank <MATH_0028> (this is a simple lemma on\nrepresentation theory of finite groups; insert future reference here).\nVia the equivalence of\nLemma <REF_0004>\nthis means <MATH_0029> is a successive extension of\nconstant sheaves with value <MATH_0030>.\nMoreover the degree of <MATH_0031> is prime to <MATH_0032>\nas it is equal to the index of <MATH_0033> in <MATH_0034>.\n<STRUCT_0002>",
